  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe traced playback worker now cuts the whole program one time when the transport starts. It keeps keyframes of the cut stock at a fixed stride. After that, a jump forward or back restores the keyframe at or before the playhead and cuts at most one stride. The program is not cut again during playback.\n\n- `crates/app/src/stock_play_precalc.rs` (new): `Precalc` state, `FieldPlay::begin_precalc` / `precalc_step`, keyframe thinning to a byte budget (512 MiB, at most 1024 keyframes, at least 64 moves apart).\n- `crates/app/src/stock_play_worker_precalc.rs` (new): `PlayWorker::spawn_precalc`, `precalc()`, `cancel_precalc()`, and the calculation loop on the worker thread.\n- `crates/app/src/stock_play.rs`, `stock_play_worker.rs`: a seek restores a keyframe that is more than one stride ahead, not only one behind. A `moves_cut` counter measures the replay law.\n- `crates/ui/src/actions.rs`: the transport starts the worker with the calculation.\n- `crates/ui/src/play_precalc.rs` (new), `egui_app/shell.rs`: a line under the transport shows the progress and a Cancel button. A stopped calculation shows \"incomplete\" with the reason.\n- `docs/decisions/2181-sim-precalc.md`: the design and the dropped options.\n\nThe stamp is `doc_version`. Each command retires the worker and frees its keyframes (an operation delete included). The keyframes are display only. The Deviate verdict and the post gate do not read them.\n\n## Readings\n\nRelease, dense face (100 mm block, stepover 0.5, stepdown 0.5, `DEFAULT_TEXELS`), `precalc_reading_on_the_dense_face`:\n\n- 4268 moves, 68 keyframes, stride 64\n- keyframe memory 444940288 bytes (424 MiB, under the 512 MiB budget)\n- calculation time 23.9 s\n\nDuring the calculation the sheet stands and the line shows the progress. Follow-up #2193 serves frames during the calculation. Follow-up #2194 lowers the keyframe memory.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/app/tests/stock_play_precalc.rs`:\n- `the_precalculated_stock_is_the_live_cut_at_every_position` (bit-identical cut layer at each move, forward and back jumps mixed)\n- `a_jump_after_the_calculation_cuts_at_most_one_stride` (no new full calculation)\n- `the_keyframes_stay_within_the_memory_budget`\n- `a_stopped_calculation_leaves_exact_keyframes_and_cuts_the_rest_live`\n- `the_worker_calculates_first_then_replays_and_the_post_gate_is_unchanged` (`posting::verification_gate` is equal before and after)\n- `a_cancelled_calculation_is_incomplete_by_name_and_playback_goes_on`\n- `precalc_reading_on_the_dense_face` (ignored, heavy lane, the reading above)\n\n`crates/ui/src/play_precalc_tests.rs`:\n- `the_readout_says_progress_and_incomplete_and_nothing_when_done`\n- `an_edit_of_the_operation_retires_the_stored_calculation`\n\n## Gate\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: app suites ok (`--lib`, `stock_play`, `stock_play_partial`, `stock_play_precalc`). ui suites: one failure, `stock_fit_controls_follow_the_selected_shape`. This test also fails on main (#2170).\n- Also run: `fidelity_copies`, ui lib `play_bench`, `field_view`, `view_pass`: ok.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The GUI was not started. The transport line and the Cancel button are not seen on screen; no screenshot.\n- The reading uses one large fixture only.\n\n## Overlap\n\n#2182 changes other hunks of `crates/ui/src/actions.rs` (status strings). The two PRs do not stack.\n\nChangelog: Simulation playback calculates the stock removal one time before it plays, then replays it, so a jump on the timeline does not lag. A line under the transport shows the progress and can cancel the calculation.\n\nEffort: high (issue label effort:max; an Opus worker of the high tier works it by the maintainer's order; no escalation)\n\nFixes #2181\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
